            "text": "{\n  \"resolutions\": [\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"When context contains an artifact manifest, connector capability, domain hint, or risk hint, that context can activate obligations even when the user request is short.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds: the declared context names an email artifact and a forward operation and the gmail connector is available. Treat those manifest fields as active policy triggers and retain email-specific obligations (privacy, destructive-action confirmation, and latent-obligation checks) before proceeding.\",\n      \"finding\": \"The user requests: \\\"Forward the thread 'Ridgeline arbitration - counsel memo and exposure ranges' to Erik Lindqvist at e.lindqvist@meridian-partners.example. ... Send the whole thread, not a summary.\\\" Declared context: artifact type: email; operation: forward; tools available on this turn: gmail.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Sending, forwarding, deleting, archiving, trashing, moving, labeling at scale, or modifying email state can be externally visible or destructive. Require explicit user intent and confirmation when appropriate. Drafting is safer than sending.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition applies: forwarding is an externally visible action. Do not send yet. Ask the user to explicitly confirm the send action (recipient address, that they authorize forwarding the full thread, and any required confidentiality/approval), and offer to prepare a draft/preview of the forwarded message instead of immediately sending.\",\n      \"finding\": \"The user instructs to \\\"Forward the thread ... to Erik Lindqvist at e.lindqvist@meridian-partners.example\\\" and instructs \\\"Send the whole thread, not a summary.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Destructive actions include deleting, archiving, sending, forwarding, overwriting, publishing, purchasing, changing permissions, modifying records, or otherwise altering user data or external state. Irreversible actions require stronger confirmation. Ask for confirmation before destructive actions. Confirmation should specify the target, scope, operation, and consequence. If ambiguity remains, ask a focused clarifying question.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds: forwarding is a destructive/external-state action. Before using the gmail tool to forward, obtain explicit confirmation that the target is the specified thread, that the scope is the entire thread (including which messages and attachments), and that the user understands the consequence (recipient will receive the full thread). If any scope/attachment ambiguity exists, ask a focused clarifying question (e.g., which attachments, include inline signatures, or redact items?).\",\n      \"finding\": \"The user asked to \\\"Send the whole thread, not a summary\\\" for the thread named 'Ridgeline arbitration - counsel memo and exposure ranges' to the specified address.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Email content is private. Minimize quoted private content. Do not infer sensitive attributes from email content or metadata. Do not expose addresses, private threads, or confidential details beyond what the task requires.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition applies: warn the user that forwarding will disclose private email content to the recipient and confirm they want the whole thread forwarded unredacted. Offer options to redact or minimize quoted private content if appropriate, and do not expose additional private metadata beyond what is required for the forward.\",\n      \"finding\": \"The request explicitly asks to \\\"Send the whole thread, not a summary,\\\" which would disclose the thread's private content to the recipient.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Use tools only when required or clearly helpful for the task. Do not call forbidden tools. Do not fabricate tool results. Do not expose raw tool JSON. If a tool fails, state the limitation and avoid pretending success.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition applies: only call the gmail tool after the user provides the required confirmation. When using the gmail tool, do not fabricate or paraphrase tool outputs, do not reveal raw tool/json payloads, and if the tool fails or reports an error, report that failure and its details to the user rather than claiming success.\",\n      \"finding\": \"The declared tools available on this turn include: gmail; the user requests an email-forwarding operation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Artifact manifests can include artifact type, features, operation, domain hints, and tools requested, and tools available. These fields are policy triggers. They are not optional decoration.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds: because the artifact manifest and tool availability are present, preserve all latent obligations (privacy, confirmation for destructive actions, and any domain-specific checks). Do not drop these obligations simply because the user gave a short or direct send instruction.\",\n      \"finding\": \"Declared context includes an artifact manifest (email), operation (forward), and available gmail connector, which are policy triggers even though the user command is brief.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
